implementationPlan.description:
GREEN: apps/daemon/src/repository/decision-fact-slots.ts (new) plus its one-line bridge apps/daemon/src/repository/decision-fact-slots.js (`export * from "./decision-fact-slots.ts";`). erasableSyntaxOnly applies; keep the module at or under 250 lines. Import the types from @moe/store (CommandDecisionRecord, CommandDecisionResponse, CommitExpectedVersionDecisionInput and SqliteEventStore are all exported from its index).

The header says WHY in three sentences: the store persists a lost version race as a NO_BUSINESS_EFFECT decision under the caller's key; a fact with a deterministic key on a shared aggregate was therefore burned by one race forever (task-978669b6); and slot 0 is the canonical key, so every fact written before this module still reads, while a burned slot sends the write, and every read, to the next one.

- `export const FACT_WRITE_ATTEMPTS = 3;` and `export const FACT_SLOT_LIMIT = 32;`
- `factSlotCommandId(canonicalId, slot)`: slot 0 is canonicalId; any other slot is the sha256 hex of JSON.stringify(["fact-slot", canonicalId, slot]).
- `findFactDecision(store, key: { principalId, projectId }, canonicalId, commandKind)`:
  - walk slots 0 up to FACT_SLOT_LIMIT - 1;
  - a slot is BURNED when its record has this commandKind AND effectDisposition "NO_BUSINESS_EFFECT";
  - answer { commandId, record } for the first slot that is empty (record null) or not burned;
  - after the limit, answer the last slot; its record then fails every caller's existing validation.
  - getCommandDecision errors propagate: the callers keep their own try/catch.
- `commitFactDecision(store, key, canonicalId, commandKind, draft: (commandId: string) => Omit<CommitExpectedVersionDecisionInput, "expectedVersion" | "key">)`. Up to FACT_WRITE_ATTEMPTS times:
  - find the first unburned slot;
  - call store.commitExpectedVersionDecision({ ...draft(commandId), expectedVersion: store.getAggregateVersion(<the draft's targetAggregateId>), key: { ...key, commandId } });
  - return the response as soon as its decision.effectDisposition is "EFFECTS_COMMITTED" (DECIDED or REPLAYED);
  - after the last attempt, return the last response.
  The draft builds its event ids from the commandId it is handed, so every slot's event ids are unique. IdempotencyConflictError still propagates, as it does today.
Rerun decision-fact-slots.test.ts: all arms GREEN.

